    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a13-a4">

                <pb facs="0399" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg389"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 4 in No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Graham to Sir P.
                        Wodehouse.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Cape Town,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your letter of this date is received, and
                    its request complied with. I have appointed Mr. J. M. Hoets, of Simon’s Town, to
                    inspect the Tuscaloosa, and report to me her present condition and equipments.
                    He is also instructed to submit this report to the admiral of the station, or
                    some one authorized to act for him, for an indorsed approval or dissent.</p>
                <p>When that report is received I will take pleasure in sending you a copy.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WALTER GRAHAM, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
